Ladybird resolves a container-relative unit against the nearest size
container that has a box, and against the small viewport where none
does. Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 (Playwright’s
build) give the same values in every case of the new test, scaled to
their 1280px viewport. Blink’s FindSizeForContainerAxis() moves on to
the next container out whenever ContainerQueryEvaluator::Width() or
Height() has no value, and WebKit’s resolveContainerUnit() goes on
calling ContainerQueryEvaluator::selectContainer() until it finds one
with an eligible RenderBox. Gecko’s ContainerSizeQuery::lookup() merges
in the next container out while query_container_size() leaves an axis
of the one it found unknown.

The engines differ on one query in the test, not a unit: For a container
hidden between an outer container and the element, Firefox answers
“@container (min-width: 300px)” from the outer container. Ladybird
answers unknown for that query, as Chrome and WebKit do.
